# Testing Conventions

## Framework
- pytest with fixtures, no unittest.TestCase
- Run: `pytest tests/ -v`

## Directory Structure
Mirror source layout:
```
tests/
  test_agents/
    test_market_analyst.py
    test_trader.py
  test_dataflows/
    test_interface.py
    test_y_finance.py
  test_graph/
    test_trading_graph.py
    test_signal_processing.py
  test_backtesting/
    test_engine.py
  conftest.py          # shared fixtures
```

## Mocking Rules
- Always mock LLM calls (`ChatOpenAI.invoke`, `ChatAnthropic.invoke`)
- Always mock external API calls (yfinance, Alpha Vantage, etc.)
- Always mock ChromaDB for memory tests
- Use `unittest.mock.patch` or `pytest-mock`

## Fixtures (conftest.py)
```python
@pytest.fixture
def sample_agent_state():
    """Provide a minimal valid AgentState for testing."""
    ...

@pytest.fixture
def mock_llm():
    """Provide a mocked LLM that returns predictable responses."""
    ...

@pytest.fixture
def sample_config():
    """Provide a test configuration based on DEFAULT_CONFIG."""
    ...
```

## Test Naming
- `test_<function>_<scenario>_<expected>` pattern
- Example: `test_process_signal_buy_returns_buy()`
